From: Robert Vokac <robertvokac@robertvokac.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] uikit: do not flip a scene window's bounds ahead of a pending
 rotation

UIKit_ComputeViewFrame swaps the UIWindow's width and height whenever the
app supports no portrait orientation but the bounds are portrait-shaped. A
UIWindow that belongs to a UIWindowScene is rotated by UIKit itself, so while
the rotation to a newly narrowed orientation set is still pending the root
view is given a landscape frame inside a portrait window; when UIKit then
rotates the window, autoresizing applies the size change to that already
swapped frame. A landscape-only game started on a portrait iPhone 17
simulator ended with a 1346x0 view and a 1-pixel-high drawable.

The swap is kept for screen bounds and for windows without a scene, which is
what the iOS 10 workaround it implements was written for.

Not an upstream commit: SDL main still swaps (checked 2026-10-08). Carried by
CNA (plans/plan_apple_m4.md AM4-120).
---
diff --git a/src/video/uikit/SDL_uikitvideo.m b/src/video/uikit/SDL_uikitvideo.m
--- a/src/video/uikit/SDL_uikitvideo.m
+++ b/src/video/uikit/SDL_uikitvideo.m
@@ -239,6 +239,18 @@
      * https://bugzilla.libsdl.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3505
      * https://bugzilla.libsdl.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3465
      * https://forums.developer.apple.com/thread/65337 */
+    /* A UIWindow that belongs to a UIWindowScene is rotated by UIKit itself, and
+     * its bounds are always the interface's current orientation. While a
+     * rotation to a newly narrowed orientation set is still pending, flipping
+     * them here gives the root view a frame of the other orientation, and
+     * UIKit's autoresizing then carries that mismatch through the rotation
+     * (a portrait 402x874 window becoming landscape left the view 1346x0).
+     * The workaround below is for screen bounds and windows without a scene. */
+    BOOL windowFollowsScene = NO;
+    if (@available(iOS 13.0, *)) {
+        windowFollowsScene = data != nil && data.uiwindow != nil && data.uiwindow.windowScene != nil;
+    }
+
 #pragma clang diagnostic push
 #pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Wdeprecated-declarations"
     UIInterfaceOrientation orient = [UIApplication sharedApplication].statusBarOrientation;
@@ -249,7 +261,7 @@
 
     /* The orientation flip doesn't make sense when the window is smaller
      * than the screen (iPad Split View, for example). */
-    if (fullscreen && (landscape != (frame.size.width > frame.size.height))) {
+    if (!windowFollowsScene && fullscreen && (landscape != (frame.size.width > frame.size.height))) {
         float height = frame.size.width;
         frame.size.width = frame.size.height;
         frame.size.height = height;
